<h2 class="g-h2" id="behaviour">Behaviour</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>Each tier row and segment carries <code>data-narrow="&lt;tier&gt;"</code>. On the opinion page, following one opens the list's tab and <code>treatment_list.js</code> narrows the list to that tier, with a removable chip naming it. Zero tiers stay in the list as plain text so the five rows always line up.</p></div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>The bar is <code>role="img"</code> with a summary ("2 stop, 1 caution, 3 neutral of 6"); its segments are out of the tab order because the rows below repeat them as links with full labels ("Caution: 1 of 6, show them").</p></div>

